open for forty-one years. Its window display changed with the seasons — snow shovels in November, box fans in June — and for most of those years the owner, Ruth, changed it herself on a Sunday morning before anyone was around to see her do it."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":"In March, the display stopped changing. The box fans stayed up through July. A hand-lettered sign appeared on the door listing new hours: closed Mondays, closed by four on Saturdays. Regular customers noticed that the shelves toward the back had gaps that did not fill in."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":"In August a second sign went up, printed this time, thanking the neighborhood for forty-one years. Two days later a commercial real estate listing appeared in the window. Ruth kept the register open through September, selling what was left at prices she wrote on masking tape by hand."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"children":"On the last afternoon, a line formed that reached past the laundromat next door. Several people in it had not bought anything at the store in years."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":["$L2d","$L2e","$L2f"]}]]}]]}]
